{"purpose":"Record the repository-discovery defect that breaks five tests on any machine whose home directory is itself a git repository, and state the acceptance criteria.","content":"## 1. Observed behaviour\n`go test ./... -short` in eka-cli fails deterministically in this environment:\n\n```\n--- FAIL: TestDiscoverEmptyDir\n--- FAIL: TestRunEmptyDirectory\n--- FAIL: TestRunExistingEkaRepoWithoutGit\n--- FAIL: TestRunStdinDevNullNonInteractive\n--- FAIL: TestRunStdinPipeNonInteractive\nFAIL github.com/maleolabs/eka-cli/v2/bootstrap\n```\n\nEvery other package passes. The failure is environmental, not flaky: it appears or disappears depending on whether a `.git` directory exists at or above the home directory.\n\n## 2. Root cause\n`bootstrap/discover.go` `detectGitRepo` walks from the target directory upward to the filesystem root looking for a `.git` entry, with no bound:\n\n```go\nfor {\n    if _, err := os.Stat(filepath.Join(dir, \".git\")); err == nil {\n        d.IsGitRepo = true\n        d.GitRoot = dir\n        return\n    }\n    parent := filepath.Dir(dir)\n    if parent == dir { return }\n    dir = parent\n}\n```\n\nIn this environment `/home/m2codeloan/.git` exists, so a fresh directory under `/tmp` reports `IsGitRepo:true` with `GitRoot:/home/m2codeloan`. Test `TestDiscoverEmptyDir` therefore observes `IsGitRepo:true` where it expects false, and the four `Run*` tests take the \"existing git repository\" branch where they expect the \"git init\" branch: `GitStatus = \"existing\", want skipped`.\n\n## 3. Impact\nBench CI is red for any contributor whose home directory is a repository — a common setup. The defect also silently misreports project scaffolding state in interactive use, which is worse than the test failures: `eka init` on a scratch directory will believe a repository already exists.\n\n## 4. Acceptance criteria\n- Repository discovery returns no git root when the walked-up `.git` belongs to a directory that encloses the user's home or is the home directory itself, or more simply: the walk terminates at a documented boundary rather than the filesystem root.\n- `eka-cli/bootstrap` tests pass in an environment where a `.git` directory exists above the test temporary directory.\n- Interactive discovery reports the same repository state that `git rev-parse --show-toplevel` reports for the target, including the no-repository case.\n- A regression test constructs a nested git repository above a temporary target and asserts discovery does not claim it."}